WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.086
Every litigation team now has access to AI.

2
00:00:04.086 --> 00:00:07.844
The hard question is whether you can trust what it says.

3
00:00:07.844 --> 00:00:10.729
LegalPrecision AI is built around one rule.

4
00:00:10.729 --> 00:00:17.440
Every finding points to the page it came from, so your team can check it before anyone relies on it.

5
00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:22.636
There are several ways to work with us, and most firms start small.

6
00:00:22.636 --> 00:00:24.474
A single document assessment.

7
00:00:24.474 --> 00:00:27.009
A review of a filing before it goes out.

8
00:00:27.009 --> 00:00:28.974
A full review of a case record.

9
00:00:28.974 --> 00:00:32.016
Support through depositions, hearings and trial.

10
00:00:32.016 --> 00:00:33.981
Appeals and post-judgment work.

11
00:00:33.981 --> 00:00:37.910
And, for firms that want it, a private workspace of their own.

12
00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:40.671
The easiest start is free.

13
00:00:40.671 --> 00:00:45.266
Send us one document, or a small sample, from a matter you choose.

14
00:00:45.266 --> 00:00:47.007
We send back three files.

15
00:00:47.007 --> 00:00:48.330
A one-page summary.

16
00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:51.743
The findings, each tied to the page it came from.

17
00:00:51.743 --> 00:00:52.857
And a scorecard.

18
00:00:52.857 --> 00:00:56.060
Then we walk you through them on a short call.

19
00:00:57.010 --> 00:01:04.278
For briefs, motions and petitions, the Precision Score checks a draft against nine elements, out of ninety points.

20
00:01:04.278 --> 00:01:06.828
Record cites are compared with the page.

21
00:01:06.828 --> 00:01:11.992
Quotations are checked word for word, and word limits are counted, not estimated.

22
00:01:11.992 --> 00:01:15.690
You get a ranked list of fixes before the filing goes out.

23
00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:22.340
For a whole case, we read the full record, including attachments, transcripts and exhibits.

24
00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:29.041
You get a dated chronology, an index of every document, and a case summary, each line linked to its source.

25
00:01:29.041 --> 00:01:34.240
Your team can then ask questions about that record, and the answers stay inside it.

26
00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:39.111
During active litigation, we support the team as the record grows.

27
00:01:39.111 --> 00:01:42.200
Each new transcript and filing is added to the case.

28
00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:51.110
Contradictions between testimony and documents are flagged, with both sources shown, so counsel can use them at the next deposition, hearing or trial.

29
00:01:52.060 --> 00:02:00.761
When a ruling goes the wrong way, we review the record and the briefing to show what was raised, what was not, and what reads differently now.

30
00:02:00.761 --> 00:02:06.460
It gives counsel a clear, sourced starting point for rehearing, appeal or post-judgment work.

31
00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:12.519
For firms that want more, we build and operate a private AI workspace for the firm.

32
00:02:12.519 --> 00:02:14.304
Your cases are kept separate.

33
00:02:14.304 --> 00:02:16.889
Your templates and standards are built in.

34
00:02:16.889 --> 00:02:20.951
And we run it, so your team does not have to become technologists.

35
00:02:20.951 --> 00:02:24.090
Most firms start with one case and grow from there.

36
00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:32.416
General AI tools are powerful, but they sell seats in a shared product, and your team is left to check the output.

37
00:02:32.416 --> 00:02:33.711
We work differently.

38
00:02:33.711 --> 00:02:35.716
Answers are linked to the page.

39
00:02:35.716 --> 00:02:38.175
Quotes are checked against the source.

40
00:02:38.175 --> 00:02:40.116
Output follows your standards.

41
00:02:40.116 --> 00:02:44.840
And errors are counted and tracked, so accuracy is measured, not assumed.

42
00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:48.310
The same method works wherever you practice.

43
00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:54.897
It has been used in criminal, appellate, family and commercial matters, in state, federal and international courts.

44
00:02:54.897 --> 00:02:57.990
Each review follows the rules of the court you are in.

45
00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:05.518
We also run a working session for litigation teams, called checking AI output against the record.

46
00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:10.740
It takes forty-five minutes, in person or online, for lawyers and paralegals.

47
00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:13.120
The boundaries are clear.

48
00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:16.267
We are not a law firm, and we do not give legal advice.

49
00:03:16.267 --> 00:03:20.902
We do not make strategy calls, and we never file or send anything on your behalf.

50
00:03:20.902 --> 00:03:22.389
Every case stays separate.

51
00:03:22.389 --> 00:03:25.250
Counsel reviews the work and makes every judgment.

52
00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:29.981
To get started, choose one document from a matter you know well.

53
00:03:29.981 --> 00:03:35.240
We will send back the summary, the findings and the scorecard, and walk you through them.

54
00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:39.080
Ask the person who shared this video, or visit legalprecision.ai.

55
00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:41.580
LegalPrecision AI.

56
00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:43.130
Organized records.

57
00:03:43.130 --> 00:03:45.110
Findings you can check.
